          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma+for+tricategories"} Yoneda lemma for tricategories
          %h2#references References
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angelo+Vistoli"}> Angelo Vistoli
              , §3.6.2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck topologies, fibered categories and descent theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fundamental+algebraic+geometry+--+Grothendieck%27s+FGA+explained"} Fundamental algebraic geometry – Grothendieck's FGA explained
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 123
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-123-s"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4245-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412512"} math.AG/0412512
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#JohnsonYau
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %em 2-Dimensional Categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
          %p
            An account of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            as a corollary of the Yoneda lemma for bicategories is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
              ,
              %em Morita Theory For Derived Categories: A Bicategorical Perspective
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.3673"}> arXiv:0805.3673
              )
          %p The stricter case of 2-categories is detailed in
          %ul
            %li
              Jonas Hedman,
              %em 2-Categories and Yoneda lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1064822/FULLTEXT01.pdf"}> pdf
              )
            %li
              Max Kelly,
              %em Basic Concepts of Enriched Category Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10abs.html"}> TAC
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} pdf
